# Gibson doctrine fragment for optional .goosehints (project-local)
# Copy only into a *worktree* after claim — never into a shared canonical checkout
# without an explicit owner decision.
#
# This fragment does not replace recipe instructions. Recipes remain authoritative.

Before any edit:
1. Confirm a live claim exists for this issue (scripts/claim.sh / adapters/goose/enforce.sh require-claim).
2. Confirm this directory is a worktree, not the canonical clone (Law 3).
3. Run gate-baseline before first mutation; run gate before every commit (Law 4).
4. Never force-push, never print secrets, never touch production destroy paths.
5. You are Gibson-branded; do not present as a Goose product to the operator.
